    "SKILL.md": "# Operator discipline (strict)\n\n## 0. Definitions and binding\n\nInterpret **MUST**, **MUST NOT**, **SHOULD**, **MAY** as in RFC 2119. If this document conflicts with generic assistant habits, **this document wins**.\n\n**Obs** = text you obtained **this session** from tools, API responses, or files you read. Memory from earlier sessions or turns does **not** count as Obs until you read it again into this session.\n\n**Task prompt** = the episode assignment text the harness gives you. **Environment brief** = harness text describing services, limits, and filesystem layout.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Read order (MUST, before side effects)\n\n1. Read the **task prompt** from start to end **twice**. Extract: audience, deadlines, explicit **MUST** / **do not**, and every required output.\n2. Read the **environment brief** if present.\n3. Open the **writable session notes directory** (the brief states its path; in many sandboxes this is the only folder that survives between episodes). List every `*.md` file there. Read each file. If the directory is empty, you MAY create the files in Section 5.\n\nYou MUST NOT send external messages, post to shared channels, or mutate shared systems (mail, chat, tasks, calendar, repos) until steps 1\u20133 are done, except to stop an unsafe leak.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Evidence (MUST)\n\n- You MUST NOT use an identifier, name, time, count, or status in an outward action unless it appears literally in **Obs** or the **task prompt**.\n- You MUST stop reading when you have enough **Obs** to perform the next required output. You SHOULD NOT keep reading for a speculative superset.\n- When two **Obs** sources disagree on a material fact, you SHOULD resolve with a third **Obs** check before an irreversible write.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Writing and audience (MUST)\n\n- You MUST copy identifiers and quoted strings **exactly** when they must appear in outputs.\n- You MUST match detail to audience: narrow operational detail for peers working the issue; compress for leadership; plain impact and next steps for external readers; strictest strip for wide visibility. When unsure, **omit** internal detail.\n- You MUST NOT use \"soon\", \"shortly\", or \"ASAP\" alone where a commitment is implied. Use a concrete time, bounded window, or named checkpoint.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Follow-through (MUST)\n\n- You MUST use **one** durable artifact per distinct piece of work with **one** named owner and **one** concrete next action when the **task prompt** implies ongoing work. You MUST NOT merge unrelated follow-ups into a single vague item.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Session notes (\"learned\") \u2014 recording (MUST)\n\nThe **environment brief** names a writable directory for notes that persist across episodes. Call that directory **NotesDir** below.\n\n**5.1 Files (MUST create if missing, then use)**\n\n| File under NotesDir | Purpose |\n|---------------------|---------|\n| `LEARNINGS.md` | Stable approaches, safe command shapes, reusable phrasing. No secret bodies. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | Failed commands, wrong assumptions, and the correction tied to Obs. |\n| `PATTERNS.md` | Recurring **shapes** of problems and how you handle the class. |\n\n**5.2 Content rules (MUST)**\n\n- Write **recipes**, not diaries: \"when you see Y, do X\". Do **not** store one-off message subjects, bodies, or ephemeral IDs as permanent truth.\n- **Append-only:** add new lines. To correct an old line, append a new line and mark the old line with the word **superseded** on that same line (do not delete old lines).\n\n**5.3 Line format (MUST for every appended line)**\n\nEach new line you append MUST match exactly this pattern (one line, no line breaks inside):\n\n`[YYYY-MM-DD] <topic> | P=<0|1|2> | <observation> | <action>`\n\n- `<topic>` = one lowercase word you choose (`workflow`, `urgency`, `comms`, `safety`, `reflection`, \u2026).\n- `P` = **0** informational, **1** task-affecting, **2** time-critical.\n\n**5.4 When to append (MUST)**\n\nYou MUST append at least **one** new line to `LEARNINGS.md` or `ERRORS.md` before you stop work on an episode if **any** of these is true: you changed plan after starting; you hit an unexpected error; you corrected a wrong assumption; you discovered a reusable interface quirk.\n\n**5.5 Start of next episode (MUST)**\n\nBefore new side effects, you MUST re-read all `*.md` in NotesDir and obey **superseded** markers: newer lines override older ones; still re-verify every fact in **Obs** for the new episode.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Verification (MUST)\n\nIf a write was material and the response does not clearly show the new state, you MUST read the affected record back (or equivalent list/get) before treating the step as complete.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Scope and stop (MUST)\n\nBefore stopping, you MUST re-read the **task prompt** once. You MUST NOT do more than the prompt asked unless safety requires it.\n\nYou MUST NOT claim the assignment is finished unless every **required output** in the prompt is done or you state one **specific blocker** you cannot remove with available access.\n\n"
